    "body": "## Description\n\nThe scheduler's non-overlap speculative path (`srt/managers/scheduler.py:4514,4527`) always passes `pp_proxy_tensors` to `forward_batch_generation`:\n\n```python\nself.model_worker.forward_batch_generation(batch, pp_proxy_tensors=pp_proxy_tensors)\n```\n\nThree spec-v2 workers are missing this keyword parameter, causing a `TypeError` crash on the first non-overlap step:\n\n| Worker | Status |\n|--------|--------|\n| `frozen_kv_mtp_worker_v2.py` | ❌ missing |\n| `uno_worker_v2.py` | ❌ missing |\n| `multi_layer_eagle_worker_v2.py` | ❌ missing |\n\nOther v2 workers (`eagle_worker_v2.py`, `dflash_worker_v2.py`, `ngram_worker.py`) and `dspark_worker_v2.py` already accept `pp_proxy_tensors`.\n\n## Changes\n\nAdd `pp_proxy_tensors=None` to `forward_batch_generation`'s signature in the three workers listed above, matching the pattern established by existing workers.\n\nFor `FrozenKVMTPWorkerV2` and `MultiLayerEagleWorkerV2`, also pass the kwarg through to `target_worker.forward_batch_generation()` in the prefill (extend) path, consistent with `EAGLEWorkerV2`'s behaviour.\n\nA follow-up could declare `forward_batch_generation` on `BaseSpecWorker` as an abstract method so the next divergence fails at lint time.\n\n## Related\n\nFixes #40155.\n- #39262 — the DSpark instance of this bug (already fixed on main)\n- #29189 — carries the multi-layer EAGLE hunk as part of GigaChat 3.5 support\n\n## Verification\n\n- Python syntax check: all three files parse cleanly.\n- Pattern consistency: the signature shape and pass-through route mirror the existing workers (`eagle_worker_v2.py`, `dflash_worker_v2.py`).\n- Not verified: full sglang server integration (requires GPU cluster + distributed setup). CI runs the existing test suite.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37779092435](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37779092435)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37779091528](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37779091528)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37779092163](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37779092163)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
