  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "CI has never run on this PR: `pr-gate` fails with `Missing required label 'run-ci'`. Could a maintainer add the `run-ci` label when convenient? Happy to fix anything the suite turns up.",
      "created_at": "2026-09-26T17:08:10Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/40355#issuecomment-5848177345",
      "id": 5848177345,
      "updated_at": "2026-09-26T17:08:10Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "li-lizhe"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Gentle follow-up: the branch has been rebased onto the latest `main`, so it's up to date and ready to run. CI still hasn't run once on this PR because `pr-gate` is waiting on the `run-ci` label. Could a maintainer add it when convenient? Happy to fix anything the suite surfaces. Thanks!",
      "created_at": "2026-10-08T15:45:03Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/40355#issuecomment-6063614222",
      "id": 6063614222,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-08T15:45:03Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "li-lizhe"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "On the CI state here, since it's a fairly broad red: the failing jobs are `PR Test (Arm64)`, `PR Test (Xeon)`, `PR Test (XPU)`, `PR Test (AMD)`, `PR Test (MLX)`, `PR Test (MUSA)` and `PR Test Extra (AMD)` — i.e. every backend in the matrix, including several this change cannot reach. `PR Test (sgl-router)` and `PR Test (PPU)` pass.\n\nThe change is confined to the frozen-kv-mtp path accepting `pp_proxy_tensors`; it doesn't touch anything backend-specific. A whole-matrix failure like this usually means the runs themselves broke rather than the patch, so I suspect these predate the PR's last commit (2026-10-08).\n\nI couldn't read the job logs on this repo to confirm the assertion, so I'm reporting what the check names show. Happy to rebase onto current main and re-run if that's preferred — just say so.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-31T09:26:47Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/40355#issuecomment-6541680240",
      "id": 6541680240,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-31T09:26:47Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "li-lizhe"
      }
    }
